int &ref = a;
ref = b; // What does this line do?`,options:["Yes, ref now points to b","No, ref remains an alias for a, but the value of b (20) is assigned to a","Causes a runtime crash","Compilation Error: re-binding reference is illegal syntax"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"A reference cannot be re-bound to another object. The assignment `ref = b` copies the value of `b` (20) into variable `a` referenced by `ref`."},{id:"u1s2q9",unitId:"unit1",setId:"u1s2",difficulty:"easy",question:"What will be the output of creating multiple objects of the following class?",code:`#include <iostream>
